WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
<v Sophie Lim>Thanks for making time, Michelle. You mentioned you are thinking of buying a condo next year.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Michelle Ng>Yes, around the middle of next year. I want to understand how to fund it before I start viewing.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Sophie Lim>Your time deposit ending 4410 matures on the 11th. One option is to keep part of it as cash for the down payment.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Michelle Ng>I would rather not sell my investments, the portfolio has done well.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Sophie Lim>Then a second option is to borrow against your portfolio with a Lombard loan, so you keep the investments. If their value falls, the bank can ask for more collateral or a repayment.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Sophie Lim>The third part is the mortgage itself. A mortgage specialist prepares a borrowing plan with you, then the property is valued and the bank does its credit checks and decides.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Michelle Ng>That makes sense. Can you introduce me to the mortgage specialist?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:16.000
<v Sophie Lim>Yes. I will refer you to the mortgage specialist this week with your goal and timeline, so you do not have to explain it again.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.000
<v Sophie Lim>I will also send you the time deposit options by Friday so you can decide before it matures.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:33.000
<v Michelle Ng>Thank you. I will gather my income and asset documents so they are ready for the specialist.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Michelle Ng>One more thing. My sale agreement for the review is in Thai with a certified English translation. Is that acceptable?

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Sophie Lim>I will ask the compliance team to confirm in writing and come back to you.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Michelle Ng>Great, thanks Sophie.
